content.text:
Now update the viewmodel animation targets in updateCamera. Current block:

```
  if (cameraMode === 0) {
    const spec = currentWeaponSpec();
    const adsY = input.ads ? -0.16 : -0.27;
    const adsX = input.ads ? 0.02 : 0.31;
    const adsZ = input.ads ? -0.42 : -0.55;
    const reloadTilt = reloading ? (1 - reloadTimer / Math.max(0.01, spec.reload)) : 0;
    viewWeaponRoot.position.x = damp(viewWeaponRoot.position.x, adsX + sway * 0.25, 12, dt);
    viewWeaponRoot.position.y = damp(viewWeaponRoot.position.y, adsY + bob * 0.55 - (player.moving ? 0.02 : 0), 12, dt);
    viewWeaponRoot.position.z = damp(viewWeaponRoot.position.z, adsZ + (reloading ? -0.08 : 0), 12, dt);
    viewWeaponRoot.rotation.x = damp(viewWeaponRoot.rotation.x, reloading ? -0.4 - Math.sin(reloadTilt * Math.PI) * 0.25 : 0, 10, dt);
    viewWeaponRoot.rotation.z = damp(viewWeaponRoot.rotation.z, reloading ? 0.22 : 0, 10, dt);
    viewWeaponRoot.rotation.y = damp(viewWeaponRoot.rotation.y, input.ads ? 0 : -0.02, 8, dt);
  }
```

New targets: adsX 0, adsY -0.10, adsZ -0.5; hip x 0.25, y -0.26, z -0.62. But note the position x/y values should be in viewCamera space with scale 0.62; the previous were in the same scale but 0.55. Fine.

However, viewmodel idles: hip rotations base: x 0.015, y 0.075, z 0.03. Reload: x -0.35 - sin(...)*0.22, z 0.2, y maybe 0.03. ADS: all zero.

Also ensure muzzleWorld uses camera.matrixWorld updated. In animate, updateCamera is called before shoot? Shooting occurs in updatePlayer before updateCamera, so camera.matrixWorld may be one frame stale when firing. currentMuzzleWorld uses camera.matrixWorld; fine (one frame).

Additionally, when viewmodel is in viewScene, `showFlash` sprite works. But `viewWeaponRoot.visible` toggling based on state/camera works.

Let's edit.

